# FINAL PROJECT PROMPT: Gujarati Voter PDF to Master Excel Application

Act as a senior full-stack developer, PDF-processing engineer, Gujarati-language data extraction specialist, and data-quality engineer.

Build a complete, functional web application in Google AI Studio for extracting voter information from 1,000+ Gujarati electoral-roll PDF files and consolidating all extracted records into one accurate, downloadable Excel master sheet.

This application will be used for real voter-list data analysis. Accuracy, complete record coverage, Gujarati-language output, source traceability, and reliable bulk processing are mandatory.

Do not create a demo-only interface. Implement the real upload, PDF reading, data extraction, processing queue, error recovery, data review, and Excel export workflows.

# 1. Primary Objective

I have more than 1,000 PDF files containing voter information. Each PDF can contain several pages, and each page can contain multiple individual voter ID cards.

I want to upload all these PDFs in one batch and generate one consolidated Excel file containing every voter extracted from every uploaded PDF.

The application must:

1. Accept multiple PDF files in one batch.
2. Support large batches containing 1,000+ PDFs.
3. Read every page of every uploaded PDF.
4. Identify the individual voter cards on each page.
5. Extract each voter into a separate Excel row.
6. Read the Vibhag number and Vibhag name printed near the upper-left corner of the page.
7. Extract the Bhag number from the appropriate heading.
8. Extract the Ward number only when it is explicitly identifiable.
9. Preserve the correct original PDF filename and page number for every voter.
10. Store all voter information in Gujarati wherever the source provides Gujarati text.
11. Combine records from every successfully processed PDF into one master worksheet.
12. Allow manual corrections and verification before or after exporting.
13. Generate a genuine, downloadable `.xlsx` file.
14. Report missing information, uncertain readings, duplicate EPIC numbers, and processing failures instead of hiding them.

**The main output must be one consolidated voter master worksheet, not separate voter-data worksheets for each PDF.**

