# 4. Required Processing Workflow

Create the following clear workflow.

## Step 1 — Upload PDF Files

Allow the user to select or drag and drop multiple PDFs, or upload a ZIP archive.

Display an upload summary before processing begins.

## Step 2 — Inspect PDF Documents

For each PDF:

1. Read the original filename.
2. Open the PDF using an appropriate PDF-processing library.
3. Detect the actual number of pages.
4. Inspect every page.
5. Determine whether the page contains embedded selectable text or scanned/image-based content.
6. Identify page-level election metadata.
7. Detect individual voter-card regions.
8. Extract every readable voter record.
9. Record the original page number.
10. Save the results into the master dataset.

Do not assume that every page contains voter cards.

Some pages may contain electoral-roll summaries, maps, polling-station details, photographs, or introductory information.

Skip pages that contain no individual voter records, but record their processing outcome when useful.

Do not generate fake voter rows from summary statistics, maps, or polling-station headings.

## Step 3 — Gujarati Text Extraction

Use this extraction strategy:

1. First attempt to extract usable embedded PDF text using a suitable PDF-parsing library.
2. If embedded text is unavailable, incomplete, or unreliable, render the relevant page or page region and use a Gujarati-capable visual text-recognition method.
3. Use a suitable Gemini multimodal model for visual extraction when required.
4. Identify individual voter cards from their visual boundaries and layout.
5. Extract each card separately using a structured data schema.
6. Validate the returned values before saving them.

Do not assume that every Gujarati PDF contains selectable text.

Do not require manual conversion of the PDFs before uploading them.

For scanned documents, use the actual rendered page content rather than relying exclusively on embedded text.

If page quality, handwriting, printing, or card boundaries prevent reliable extraction, mark the record or page for review.

